-- title:
--   Completed stalks away from q are integrally closed domains
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q \ge 5$, let $\ell$ be a prime with $\ell \ge 3$ and $\ell \neq q$, and let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$. Let $A_0$ be a discrete valuation domain whose maximal ideal is the principal ideal generated by the image of $q$, with finite residue field. Assume: `hℓ`, that for every $A_0$-algebra $T$ the predicate `IsLevelPStructure` at $\ell$ (two affine points $P,Q$ on $W$ whose $x$-coordinates are roots of $W.\mathrm{pre}\Psi_\ell$ and whose `indepElt` expressions are units) is preserved by Weierstrass variable changes acting on level-$P$ data; `hM`, that `IsGamma0PowAt` (the two-torsion kernel condition for $p^k = 2$, and otherwise the cyclic-kernel conditions on a monic-in-degree $\varphi(p^k)/2$ divisor $h$ of $W.\mathrm{pre}\Psi_{p^k}$) is preserved by `kernelVariableChangeDeg`; a family $\mathcal G$ of relative group laws on the graded projective models of Weierstrass curves with unit discriminant over $A_0$-algebras that is chord–tangent (realised on points over fields by an addition- and Galois-equivariant identification with the affine point group) and has origin identity; a level transport $\mathcal T$ for raw Drinfeld pairs at $q$ satisfying `IsSectionTransport`, i.e. its variable-change and coefficient-change operations commute with the induced maps on `Proj` for the two sections; and `hVC`, `hCO`, the existence of graded ring homomorphisms realising variable changes and coefficient changes on `projModelGradingCR`, compatible with the irrelevant ideals. Let $P_0$ be a package representing the moduli datum attached to `rigidDataPow`, whose points over $T$ are Weierstrass curves over $T$ with unit discriminant equipped with a $\Gamma_0$-tuple of cyclic kernel polynomials over the primes dividing $M'$, a level-$P$ structure at $\ell$ and a Drinfeld pair at $q$, taken modulo variable change: thus $B_0 = P_0.B_0$ carries a universal point such that every point over an $A_0$-algebra $T$ is induced by a unique $A_0$-algebra homomorphism $B_0 \to T$. Assume $B_0$ is of finite type over $A_0$, and let $\mathfrak m$ be a maximal ideal of $B_0$ not containing the image of $q$. Then the $\mathfrak m$-adic completion of $B_0$ is a domain, is integrally closed, and the image of $q$ in it is nonzero.
--
--   This is the generic-fibre half of the normality statement for the fine full-level moduli ring: at maximal ideals lying over the generic point of the discrete valuation base, the completed stalk of the coarse coordinate ring $B_0$ is an integrally closed domain in which the uniformiser is invertible. It feeds the flatness and normality statement for quotients by minimal primes of the same package.
